    "suggested_action": "replace_ja_expression",
    "reason": "The English lemma 'care' (noun) is very broad, encompassing meanings like 'attention', 'concern', 'provision of needs' (e.g., child care, elderly care), and 'medical treatment'. The Japanese expression '治療' (chiryou) is exclusively focused on 'medical treatment' or 'therapy'. While 'care' can sometimes mean 'medical care', '治療' is too narrow to represent the general concept of 'care' for a learner in a daily life context. A general learner encountering 'care' would likely expect a word covering broader meanings like 'looking after' or 'attention', not just medical treatment.",
